# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output and other generated files.
#
# Nothing under here is source. Every pattern project can regenerate all of
# it from the files that are committed: `./gradlew build` for the compiled
# classes, `video/build_video.sh` for the slides and the video, and
# `docs/make_animation_audio.sh` for the animation clips. Keeping the output
# out of the repository is what stops a push failing on GitHub's file-size
# limits -- a single rendered video is around 26 MB, and there is one per
# pattern.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Gradle / Maven / Java ---
build/
target/
out/
bin/
.gradle/
!gradle/wrapper/
*.class
*.war
*.ear
hs_err_pid*
replay_pid*

# --- Rendered video output -------------------------------------------------
# video/build/ holds the per-scene slide PNGs, and the mp4, m4a and srt next to
# them are the finished deliverables -- uploaded to YouTube rather than
# committed. video/poster.png is the exception: it is the YouTube thumbnail as
# well as the opening title card, it is only ~80 KB, and it is wanted in the
# repository alongside docs/thumbnail.png. See each project's video/README.md.
**/video/build/
**/video/*.mp4
**/video/*.m4a
**/video/*.srt
**/video/*.wav
**/video/*.aac

# --- Generated narration for the interactive animation ---------------------
# docs/audio/ holds one short m4a per step of docs/animation.html, produced by
# docs/make_animation_audio.sh from the narration in that script. It is the
# largest generated thing left in the tree (~1.7 MB per project), and it is
# output rather than source, so it is not committed. Anyone who wants the
# narration runs the script.
#
# The diagrams in docs/images/ and each project's docs/thumbnail.png are
# deliberately NOT ignored: nothing rebuilds them on GitHub, so ignoring them
# would leave the docs rendering with broken images, and the thumbnail ships
# alongside docs/youtube.md by convention.
**/docs/audio/

# Loudness measurements cached by gradle-java/docs/make_specs.py; derived,
# and keyed on each MP4 the specs are generated from.
gradle-java/docs/.loudness-cache.json

# Scratch directory used by gradle-java/docs/make_diagrams.py while it hands a
# single mermaid block to mermaid-cli. It holds one .mmd, one .png and the
# renderer config, all overwritten on every diagram, and none of it is source.
gradle-java/.tmp-diag/

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# --- Editors and OS ---
.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
.vscode/
.settings/
.classpath
.project
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
